    [BugFix][P/D] Handle hybrid cache views in preempt offload (#18140)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Fix preempt-offload registration for hybrid KV caches: retain the
    largest same-pointer attention view per logical block (including
    block-size scaling), deduplicate identical Mamba views separately from
    attention, and skip empty tensors. Preserve circular-buffer state as one
    private block during offload and restore. Add regression coverage and
    explicit type annotations.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Three GPQA Diamond runs on Ascend A5 with Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, P/D TP2,
    MTP3, concurrency 64, D max-num-batched-tokens 256, temperature 1, top-p
    0.95, and max output length 35,000:
    
    | D memory utilization | Accuracy | Offload events | Requests offloaded
    |
    | --- | --- | --- | --- |
    | 0.49 (run 1) | 82.83% (164/198) | 304 | 93 |
    | 0.49 (run 2) | 81.82% (162/198) | 264 | 91 |
    | 0.90 (baseline) | 80.81% (160/198) | 0 | 0 |
    
    All 198 requests completed successfully in each run. Run 1 contained one
    garbled response; no comparable garbling was found in run 2 or the
    baseline. These sampled runs do not establish numerical equivalence. The
    final typing-only cleanup was checked statically.
    
    Ruff lint/format, Python syntax, and diff whitespace checks passed. Mypy
    was not run locally. The A5 runs cover the Qwen hybrid path, not
    circular-buffer models.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
